  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 325 AM EDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nAs the Bermuda high establishes itself off the Atlantic Coast, we'll \nset up in a typical summertime pattern with SSW flow that will \nslowly but surely push temperatures back up into the low to mid 90s \nfor the rest of the forecast period; with triple digit heat index \nvalues returning this weekend. As overnight lows climb into the mid \n70s, we'll need to keep an eye on the possibility of issuing a heat \nadvisory. \n\nFortunately, afternoon thunderstorms will be expected each afternoon \nwhich may help ease temperatures during peak heating. There is \npretty good agreement that afternoon convection will form everyday \nfor the foreseeable future and there isn't anything to indicate \nwe'll be seeing a change in atmosphere anytime soon.",
